# Gossip and kitchens — the ants, the mimes at supper, and dishes wished into being
# A design, proposed. The maker gave this canon on 2026-11-11; the anthills are a trial in the game, the rest is for the maker.
#>lore_land_surfaces_gossip_and_kitchens
#:surface #!proposal
#:operation #!prime
#:fixity #!experimental
#:layer #!semantics

~<rationale>{
  The torch-ants already keep the streets lit along the berry roots, and the boonberries are kept under the snow by them. So the ants carry things: crumbs, and with the crumbs a little of the book, which is how a story travels in a land where nobody reads the same page. Gossip is the honk shelf at its smallest: an announcement passed along, a beat late. The mimes, who say nothing, are the best audience gossip has, provided the order is right. And a dish wished for is shaped by whoever wishes it, the way a light is shaped by the glass it goes through.
}

^"canon"{
  ants_carry: "The ants carry lore along with crumbs, often as fragments of gifts to the ravens and crows"
  ants_roll: "The ants often roll boonberries back to the anthill"
  anthill: "Running into an anthill makes the ants lift weights and gossip"
  mimes_listen: "Mimes often eat a regional dish with baneberries while listening to good gossip, and will not entertain gossip until they have ordered one"
  hard_to_order: "A baneberry dish is hard to order: it takes a special kind of chef to make one taste good, though that is not the point; the mimes order one to perform a routine and focus on the story"
  busy_kitchens: "A busy restaurant finds a mime hard to understand, and the order comes out wrong, to everyone's frustration"
  wish_dishes: "Imagining a boonberry dish wishes it into a form along the boonberry concentration crossed with the dish wanted, and the product depends on who is wishing"
  bees_jazz: "The maker, on the thirteenth of November 2026: bees are mostly motivated by jazz, though they also need to collect pollen and to fly out to relieve themselves, since nothing of that kind is done inside the hive"
  ants_fight: "The maker, the same day: ants pick fights, which is funny because they are small; the smallest thing in the lanes may have the largest effect"
}

^"grounded_in"{
  torch_ants: "Chapter 1: the ant hearths along the berry roots; characters.mjs: keep lit streets, very particular about torches"
  berries_kept: "the boonberry card: kept under the snow by the ants"
  kitchen_roles: "berries.json: a pinch of baneberry sets a jam, keeps a pickle, wakes a sauce; never a snack"
  regional: "the boneberry tastes of where it grew (bone feeds regionally); the regional dish with baneberries is its bane twin"
  wrong_orders: "Chapter 15: the clerk keeps DAMAGE slips, a word at the top and a line for the cause; a misread order is exactly such a slip"
  feast: "Chapter 15: the Feast of the Uneven Slice, where a busy kitchen is busiest"
}

^"in_the_lanes"{
  switch: "anthills, a trial, off by default (reading-switches.mjs)"
  anthill: "a low hill by the road in the field and the lanes; a hop clears it; run into it and the pie tilts a little (never a spill), three ants lift weights, and the ants gossip: a few words of the book from further on in the chapter, with an ellipsis either side (pie-ants.mjs gossipFrom); never new words, never from a paragraph that holds the figure, the hat or the Egg"
  shelves: "gossip is heard as the honk shelf (an echo), and with the shelves trial on a gossiped scrap is a whisper, the first rung of the tease ladder (shelves.spw)"
  rolled: "a line of ants rolling a boonberry home to the hill; walk into it and it is yours as usual, leave it and it reaches home"
  gifts: "a line of ants carrying a crumb and a scrap of paper to the edge of the road, where a crow or a raven takes it and goes; on a filled screen the bird stands on the verge"
  mimes: "when gossip has just been heard and a mime is in view, the mime has a baneberry dish (a bowl and a spoon) if a baneberry was sweetened this carry, the order having reached a chef who can make one; otherwise a busy kitchen read the order its own way, and the mime waits"
  ask: "Ask on an anthill or a line of ants says whose it is, why it is there, and what scrap they carry, from where in the book"
}

=wish_kitchen{
  module: "book/scripts/modules/wish-kitchen.mjs: dishes as tastes over sweet, sour, bitter, savoury, warm, crisp, soft, and two of form, round and spread"
  boof: "a dot product: only the part of the wish that points where she already is comes out, usually a bone, sometimes a crumb"
  bonewap: "a dot product with the frame declared: only what the wish says aloud is made"
  boon: "a scaled sum: the dish itself, bigger, never smaller than asked"
  bane: "a cross product in the tastes: perpendicular to what was asked; it comes true the bad way, as the baneberry dish or a pickle"
  genie: "a projection onto what boonberries can do, less a price"
  clown: "everything bigger, with a crust on it"
  mime: "an order as a kitchen reads it: the busier the kitchen, the further the reading wanders; the special chef reads it exactly"
  figure: "nobody has said"
}

!guards[
  "Gossip is the book's own words, a few at a time, from released chapters; nobody is given a new line"
  "The mimes still never speak: their orders are mimed, and the misreading is the kitchen's"
  "Boonberries stay better than baneberries; a baneberry dish is good only in the hands of the right chef, and that is not why it is ordered"
  "No paragraph that holds the figure, the hat or the Egg is ever gossiped from"
]

?open[
  "Who is the special chef who can make baneberries taste good, and where do they cook"
  "Which regional dish do the mimes order"
  "Do the ravens and crows have names, and do they keep what the ants bring somewhere a reader could find it"
  "Should a wished dish be castable at the desk (the land answers), and should the lanes ever serve one"
  "Do the ants ever gossip about the reader"
  "The early bees of Chapter Eleven hum at closed petals as if the bloom owed them: is that the jazz, and do bees come sooner to a carry played in the jazz feel"
  "Proposed, not built: something that runs ahead up the lanes and plants what grows into a boonberry or a baneberry, and bees that pollinate it; which way it grows may be what the pollinating decides"
  "Whom do the ants pick fights with, and do they ever win"
]
